        "original_id": "bee167a5-cec7-5bc1-9f12-4c183b44a8d8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Regency Road, Adelaide; Klemzig; Dudley Park; Adelaide; Kilkenny; Broadview\n- Roads and transport: Muller Road; North East Road; Simpson Avenue; Harrison Road; Adelaide-Gawler railway line\n- Organizations: Arndale Shopping Centre; City of Port Adelaide Enfield\n- Species: Garrha limbata\n- Places: Queensland; New South Wales; Australian Capital Territory; Victoria; South Australia\n\nFacts:\n- Regency Road in Adelaide is located about 6 km north of the city centre.\n- Regency Road in Adelaide runs from Arndale Shopping Centre in Kilkenny in the west to Broadview in the east.\n- Regency Road continues eastward as Muller Road and ends at North East Road in Klemzig.\n- Klemzig is a suburb of Adelaide in the City of Port Adelaide Enfield.\n- Dudley Park is bordered by Regency Road to the north, Simpson Avenue to the south, the Adelaide-Gawler railway line to the east, and a north-south line from the Harrison Road-Simpson Avenue intersection to Regency Road to the west.\n- Garrha limbata has been recorded in Australia from Queensland, New South Wales, the Australian Capital Territory, Victoria, and South Australia.",
